{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"b412ba67-1eb0-4a71-ac59-00f81425ce8d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The FEATHER paper headings have a different format. Let me just read the excerpt that was in the search results, which mentions that \"distribution networks like Benes in SIGMA or fat-tree in MAERI necessitate unicast or multicast capabilities to direct data from relevant on-chip buffer banks to specific PEs, and FEATHER replaces distribution NoC with pt-to-pt connections.\"\n\nI think I now have enough evidence to write a comprehensive answer. Let me consolidate everything and write the answer file.\n\nLet me now summarize my evidence for each chain node:\n\n**S1 (NoC Topology - Mesh/Torus/Tree/Butterfly):**\n- 2D mesh: HD-MoE paper, gem5/Garnet note, 2D Mesh NoC note, Meta MTIA 2i (custom NoC 8x8)\n- Active interposer: mesh topology for interposer\n- FEATHER: mentions fat-tree, crossbar, Benes (butterfly) as distribution NoCs; uses pt-to-pt instead\n- Torus: mentioned in knowledge notes as topology option in gem5/Garnet\n- Note: Specific comparison of all topologies for ML accelerators is limited\n\n**S2 (Routing & Flow Control):**\n- XY routing: HD-MoE, gem5/Garnet, 2D Mesh NoC\n- Deadlock-free: CDG (Channel Dependency Graph), turn restrictions (MTR), VC isolation (DeFT), DFBM\n- Flow control: credit-based, virtual cut-through, wormhole\n- Meta MTIA 2i: leaky-bucket traffic shaping, non-blocking architecture\n- Mugi: 3-channel NoC (input/weight/output), output-stationary\n\n**S3 (MoE All-to-All):**\n- HD-MoE: 2D mesh NoC, all-to-all dispatch/combine, XY routing, discrete-event simulation\n- Communication patterns: Intra-Expert (TP, all-reduce) vs Inter-Expert (EP, all-to-all)\n- Node-Link Balance co-optimization, Bayesian Optimization for mapping\n- Pre-broadcast strategy for dynamic scheduling\n- 2D Mesh NoC note: 25-75 GB/s per link, 4x4/4x8/8x8 mesh sizes\n\n**S4 (DiT Denoising Data Passing):**\n- No direct note evidence for DiT-specific NoC design\n- General principles: iterative computation flow, could use temporal/spatial pipelining over NoC\n- Inferences from systolic array dataflow papers\n\n**S5 (Multimodal Multi-Encoder Aggregation):**\n- Focus paper: systolic-array accelerator for VLM, on-chip concentration\n- FlashFuser: kernel fusion via inter-core NoC for Transformer\n- Limited direct NoC + multimodal evidence\n\n**S6 (Video Spatiotemporal Cross-PE Transfer):**\n- Focus paper: VLM video processing, spatiotemporal attention\n- No direct NoC + video evidence in notes\n\n**S7 (Concurrency Performance Impact):**\n- HD-MoE: communication overhead modeling, LP formulation\n- gem5/Garnet: cycle-accurate latency, throughput, saturation\n- Meta MTIA 2i: 3.3x bandwidth, non-blocking, flow control\n\nNow let me write the answer following the required structure for L6 and the \"硬件架构和运行时\" priority.\n\nFor the L6 (chip design) granularity, I need:\n1. Mermaid flowchart of chip topology (chiplet interconnect, die-to-die interface)\n2. Evaluation table (process node, die area, power, interconnect protocol, bandwidth, TOPS/W)\n3. Annotations for each diagram/table\n\nLet me start writing now.","signature":"b412ba67-1eb0-4a71-ac59-00f81425ce8d"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":84869,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":28032,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9022b13a-f534-46e0-975c-ed63ef64f9c3","uuid":"cc17e5fb-8575-4ccf-be7c-6308993ae468"}
